-- title:
--   Geometric normality of the chart ring L ⊗_R C
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian unique factorisation domain, let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be an intermediate field of the extension $K_0 \subseteq K_0(\!(q)\!)$ of Laurent series over $K_0$, equipped with an $R$-algebra structure making $R \to K_0 \to F$ a tower. Let $j \in F$ be non-zero and transcendental over $R$, and assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ generated by $j$ over $K_0$. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin R ↥F j` for the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j]$ generated by $j$, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. Finally let $L$ be any field that is simultaneously a $K_0$-algebra and an $R$-algebra, compatibly with $R \to K_0$. Then the $R$-algebra tensor product $L \otimes_R C$ is an integral domain and is integrally closed in its field of fractions.
--
--   This is the assertion that the affine chart ring $C$ of the two-chart integral model has geometrically normal generic fibre: after any field base change over $K_0$ it remains a normal domain. It is used in the construction of the auxiliary full-level modular curve models, where $L \otimes_R C$ is identified with a concrete ring over an algebraically closed field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_tensorProduct_chartAlgFin_of_le_laurentSeries.lean

